Let me think step by step. For two_sum on sorted array, the hashmap approach is O(n) time and O(n) space. For sorted input we can use two pointers for O(1) extra space.

For two_sum on sorted array I will use a hash map from value to index and check complements in one pass.

```python
def two_sum(nums, target):
    seen = {}
    for i, n in enumerate(nums):
        if target - n in seen:
            return [seen[target - n], i]
        seen[n] = i
    return [-1, -1]
```

